+# Naga V3 Pro device illustration
+
+User-requested AI-assisted composite for this downstream test build, created
+with the built-in imagegen tool on 2026-09-26. This is an edited illustration,
+not an unmodified official Razer photograph. The V2 model image is unchanged.
+The PNG retains transparency and is packaged locally, independent of image caches.
+
+Inputs:
+
+- V3 mouse: https://medias-p1.phoenix.razer.com/sys-master-phoenix-images-container/hf7/he7/10268566880286/naga-v3-pro-500x500.png
+- V2 spare-plate/composition reference: https://dl.razerzone.com/src2/6292/6292-1-en-v1.png
+
+Final prompt:
+
+> Use case: compositing. Asset type: transparent PNG device illustration for Polychromatic's hardware panel. Image 1 is the edit target: the actual Razer Naga V3 Pro mouse. Image 2 is a composition reference and supporting insert: the two detached interchangeable side plates at the left of the Naga V2 Pro. Create the V3 equivalent of that presentation: retain the V3 mouse from Image 1, with its exact silhouette, buttons, wheel, green markings, logo, proportions and existing viewing angle unchanged; add the two detached side plates from Image 2 to its left, six-button plate at far left and two-button plate next, at a matching physical scale. There should be exactly one V3 mouse with its installed twelve-button side, plus exactly two separate spare plates. Do not substitute the V2 mouse body, redesign the V3, add cables or a dongle, or add labels/text/watermark. Reframe the canvas only as needed to fit all three objects, keeping generous even margins and the object group centered like Image 2. Preserve the photographed matte-black materials and fine details. Deliver a genuinely transparent background with alpha, not a white or checkerboard background.
